WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:07.540
The one thing you may have noticed first in
this trailer is that they never show off Pennywise's

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.380
face in full, it's always obstructed by something.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:14.120
But after going through frame by frame, I
found a subliminal message that plays for

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.030
1/12th of a second, so stick around if you
want to see that.

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:20.240
This opening scene with the boat seems to
show that this will be super faithful to the

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:21.350
source material.

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:24.610
This box of tissues shows us that Bill is
sick when he makes the boat.

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:26.400
These curtains tell us that they are in the
50s.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.690
There seems to be a pad and pencils on Bill's
bed, perhaps a nod to the fact that Bill grows

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.270
up to be a writer in the book.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:36.909
He also seems quite interested in astronomy,
though I'm not sure what to make of that.

00:00:36.909 --> 00:00:39.220
Let me know your interpretation in the comments.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:42.379
As Georgie is playing with his boat, we see
that the streets of Derry seem to be covered

00:00:42.379 --> 00:00:45.079
with these tents, which are blocked off by
Public Works.

00:00:45.079 --> 00:00:48.760
It looks like they may have been used to cover
up the sewage caps in the street, which may

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.370
be a result of IT.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:54.100
With sandbags all around the base of these
tents, it seems they don't want anything getting

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.409
in or out.

00:00:55.409 --> 00:00:59.319
Glad to see this scene in here, I know all
too many people who refuse to walk near sewer

00:00:59.319 --> 00:01:00.899
grates because of this part.

00:01:00.899 --> 00:01:05.030
It's obviously dark in there, but it seems
Pennywise may not have his signature balloons.

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:08.500
There are two big red arrows on the ground
pointed at this monument.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.200
Here we see a woman putting up missing posters
for Patrick Hockstetter.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:16.450
Patrick is one of the bullies in Henry Bowers'
gang who terrorizes The Losers Club.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:21.030
In the 1990 TV mini-series, he is basically
just a minor character, but in the book, he

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.940
is probably the most disturbing human character
of all.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:27.340
I'm going to steer clear of spoilers, but
if you've read the book, you know that things

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:28.980
are about to get dark.

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:33.180
Also, look how many staples are on this post,
just think about all the missing kids in this

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.490
town that have already been given up on.

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:39.890
This is obviously the library scene, but as
I recall, this scene took place when they

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:41.680
were adults, not kids.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:45.440
It was also Richie who sees Pennywise and
the balloons in the library in the mini-series

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:46.440
at least.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:49.730
Judging by his weight, I'd say that this character
is supposed to be Ben.

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:54.630
As a disclaimer, there may be things I'm forgetting
from the book, please drop me a comment if

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:55.810
that is the case.

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:59.770
But the point is, that throughout the entirety
of this trailer, we seem to only see the characters

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:04.990
as kids, leading me to believe that the adult
portions of the story may be cut out, or Warner

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.800
Bros. is planning to do a sequel.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:11.130
Look at this shirt he's wearing, this is clearly
a reference to Stephen King's book, Christine.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.030
The one with the killer cars.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:17.300
This house is probably 29 Neibolt Street,
a run down house in the book where the kids

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.870
encounter IT in some of it's other forms.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:24.040
In fact, it's basically confirmed a few moments
later when we see Neibolt St on this map of

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:25.310
the sewer system.

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:29.260
Speaking of which, we can also see that a
sewage line runs through the cemetery, which

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:34.780
means we may get a new adaptation of the grave
digging scene, so take your pick ba-ba-ba-Billy

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:37.800
boy, except for the one the end.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:39.760
That's already taken.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:40.840
Sorry.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:44.160
It's not really clear what's going on here,
but they are basically using their projector

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:48.410
to display a map of Derry onto a map of the
sewer lines so they can see exactly where

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:51.430
the sewers line up with actual locations in
the town.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:55.620
Here we see one of kids taking a puff of his
inhaler, which means that his character is

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:58.300
probably Eddie, the asthmatic of the group.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:02.040
In the book, the inhaler becomes a weapon
used against Pennywise, and it's presence

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:04.960
here suggests that that may still be the case.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.230
Earlier in the trailer we see them putting
slides in the projector.

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:10.990
This slide clearly says Made In USA.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:16.290
Then later on, it shows a slide popping out,
and if you look closely it says Made In Canada.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:20.520
Beverly wears a key around her neck and Ben
has solar systems on his shirt, a possible

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:23.020
connection to the planets in Bill's room.

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:26.349
For the rest of the trailer from this point
on, they cut to these two frames of the blank

00:03:26.349 --> 00:03:30.510
wall upon which they were showing the projection
in between shots, if you were wondering what

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:31.510
that was.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:35.520
If you look closely at Pennywise's reflection
right here, you'll notice that IT's eyes don't

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:39.290
seem to reflect in the water, which is pretty
creepy if you ask me.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:43.180
You'll also notice the washer and dryer right
here, which means they aren't in sewer in

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:46.270
this scene, they are in somebody's flooded
basement or something.

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:50.090
And finally the last shot of the trailer,
we see this wall again for 1/12th of second

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:55.940
and the projector is now showing our first
totally unobstructed view of Pennywise's face.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:57.050
And that's IT.

00:03:57.050 --> 00:03:58.080
Pun intended.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:01.020
If you are excited for this movie, then give
this video a like.

